msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/debian/debian.rst:93
#: 1f4a6a9970684db8a693a05cf14983aa
msgid ""
"Where you **DO** want the service to run, put this in ``/rw/config/rc."
"local``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/debian/debian.rst:102
#: b26c8d9b8bfb406aa9b7827d97169913
msgid "Don’t forget to make the file executable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/debian/debian.rst:105
#: 233d3b0b441c489aa6784d88ca62a375
msgid "Unattended Upgrades"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/debian/debian.rst:108
#: 5e2a0026dbe54e0b8f9837ff91279574
msgid ""
"Some users have noticed that on upgrading Debian templates, the ``unattended-"
"upgrade`` package is installed. This package is pulled in as part of a "
"Recommend chain, and can be purged. The lesson is that you should carefully "
"look at what is being installed to your system, particularly if you run "
"``dist-upgrade``."
msgstr ""

